================================================================================
DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI AutomationListPage shipped at parity with the web source: an
@Observable AutomationListPageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injected
AutomationListDataSource whose two methods mirror the ported web hooks verbatim (useAutomations,
useBulkAutomationsUpdate). The page reproduces the web PageContainer chrome (title + subtitle),
the shared bulk-action toolbar (selection count + noun + of-total + Enable / Disable / Delete with
a destructive confirm + Clear, each with its own spinner), and the single GlassPanel automations
table (master select-all tri-state + per-row select, name link, description, run count, and the
enabled/disabled status badge) — built on the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (TSGlassPanel /
TSButton / TSBadge / TSEmptyState / TSQueryError / TSSkeleton / TSPageTitle), no hand-rolled glass;
adaptive macOS/iPad columnar grid vs iPhone-compact card list; every visible string from
Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names; VoiceOver labels/traits (select-all, per-row,
selectAutomation), Dynamic Type, and a retryable error region so no region renders blank. Verified
on BOTH idioms by real iOS-18 + macOS-15 Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0 on the
surface), a macOS-15 XCTest typecheck (0), and an executed 21/21 model harness. The full xcodebuild
scheme is RED (** BUILD FAILED **) ONLY due to the pre-existing, out-of-scope, repo-wide Swift 6.3.2
#Preview explicit-return breakage across 157 *.Previews.swift files (forbidden to commit-fix) — the
identical disposition under which the sibling automations pages were accepted DONE.

